# FuckClaude Project Conventions

## Tech Stack & Architecture
- **Framework**: Astro (SSG/SSR hybrid via `@astrojs/vercel`) + TypeScript.
- **Production Domain**: `https://fuck-claude.vercel.app` (canonical). Custom domains (`fuckclaude.tech`, `www.fuckclaude.tech`) 308 redirect to this origin.
- **Styling**: Scoped CSS using site-wide CSS variables (`var(--surface)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--accent)`, `var(--mono)`, etc.).
- **Mobile header**: The shared `.nav` / `.nav__actions` / `.brand__text` styles live in `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro`. At `max-width: 560px` the brand collapses to the logo and `.nav__actions` wraps onto a second row. New header items must not break this; verify `documentElement.scrollWidth === viewport width` at 320/360/375/414px on `/`, `/zh/`, `/guides/`, `/news/`.
- **Grids and long tokens**: Use `minmax(min(Npx, 100%), 1fr)` for `auto-fill` grids, and `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on cards that render user-facing text with long identifiers (env vars, model names).

## Bilingual & i18n
- Supported languages: `zh` (paths prefixed with `/zh/`) and `en` (paths at `/`).
- All user-facing strings must be defined in `src/i18n/ui.ts` for both languages.
- Breadcrumbs, alternate hreflang links, and JSON-LD must stay in sync across `/zh/` and root versions.
- Automatic client/server redirects based on browser language are strictly forbidden per Google SEO guidelines.
- Use `src/components/LocaleSuggestBanner.astro` to render a non-blocking suggestion banner when browser language differs from current page language.

## News & Community Content
- **News**: Maintained in `src/config/news.ts`. Items include bilingual title, summary, takeaway, category tag, and source link. `publishedAt` must match the date on the cited source page (for example the Transparency Hub's "Last updated" date), not the date the item was added.
- **Non-official news items** (media or community reports, such as regional ban waves): cite the original publisher in `sourceName`, cross-check at least two independent sources, and state that Anthropic has not confirmed causes or scale. Do not cite vendor blogs that sell a competing service as the sole source.
- **Social / X Community Posts**: Maintained in `src/config/community-posts.ts` and rendered via `src/components/CommunityPosts.astro`. Must retain direct links to original X posts, author name, handle, profile link, tags, and practical takeaways. Verify each post before adding it (author, date, text) through `https://api.fxtwitter.com/<handle>/status/<id>`. Never add posts that cannot be verified, and do not repeat advice that tells users to open replacement accounts after a ban. Available tags are defined in `POST_TAGS`; each tag also needs a `data-tag` colour rule in `CommunityPosts.astro`.
- **News filtering**: `ClaudeNews.astro` and `getLatestNews()` accept `categories`; the guides hub shows only `policy` and `security` items, after the guide catalog.
- **Community post links**: Every post in `community-posts.ts` sets `relatedGuideSlug`; `CommunityPosts.astro` renders it as a "Related guide" link.

## Guides
- **Single source of truth**: `src/config/guides.ts` holds all guide metadata (slug, category, bilingual title/summary, `publishedAt`, `updatedAt`, optional `verifiedAt`, curated `related`, `sources`, `listed`). `updatedAt` exists only there. Bodies live in `src/content/guides/*.ts` and are registered in `src/content/guidesData.ts` as `GUIDE_CONTENT`. Adding a guide means touching those three places.
- **Pages**: `/guides/`, `/zh/guides/`, and the article routes are thin wrappers around `GuidesHubPage.astro` and `GuideArticlePage.astro` (both take `lang`). The hub catalog is `GuideCatalog.astro`; the official-rules block is `OfficialRules.astro`. Do not copy these pages per language.
- **Official facts**: Statements about Anthropic policy (supported regions, ban reasons, appeals, accepted payment methods, rate limits, transparency numbers) must link to an official page through `OFFICIAL_SOURCES` in `guides.ts`. `src/config/official-rules.ts` feeds the hub block; re-check it and bump `OFFICIAL_RULES_CHECKED_AT` and the guide's `verifiedAt` whenever one of those facts changes. Region facts must also match `https://www.anthropic.com/supported-countries` and `src/config/signals.ts`.
- **No unsourced numbers**: Do not publish card BINs, "success rate" or "pass rate" figures, or savings percentages without a source. Label community observations as such. Do not recommend specific card types or BINs as "safe", and do not promise that any setup avoids bans.
- **Hidden guides**: `listed: false` keeps a guide reachable by URL but removes it from the hub, home page, and related lists (`claude-ai-content-watermarking`).
- **Article HTML**: Bodies are HTML strings. `prepareArticleHtml()` in `src/utils/guide-html.ts` adds heading ids, builds the table of contents, and wraps every `<table>` in `.table-scroll`; do not add your own table wrappers. Dates use `YYYY-MM-DD` (`YYYY-MM` is padded to the first of the month for JSON-LD).
- **Chinese punctuation**: Chinese text uses full-width punctuation (，。？！；：). Keep ASCII punctuation inside code, identifiers, and English phrases.

## Sponsors
- **Sponsors Config**: Maintained in `src/config/sponsors.ts` and rendered via `src/components/Sponsors.astro`. Logos live under `public/sponsors/`. Entries include bilingual headlines, taglines, CTAs, and referral URLs. Sponsor copy describes the product neutrally and must not promise to bypass Claude risk control or avoid bans.

## Detection Signals
- Fingerprint detection signals live in `src/config/signals.ts` with sum of weights = 100.
- Detection must run client-side only without uploading user data. Follow `skills/detection-signals/SKILL.md`.
